  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering UI State Variables**\n\nI\'m currently integrating variables like `isSidebarCollapsed` and `isMobileSidebarOpen` within `ui-store.ts`. The aim is to ensure stable sidebar widths on desktops (either 240px or 64px when collapsed) and responsive behavior on mobile/tablets (< 768px). The goal is to provide a consistent and usable interface across different screen sizes.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m now focusing on mobile and tablet responsiveness within `Sidebar.tsx` and `AppTopBar.tsx`. The aim is to implement a sliding overlay drawer for the sidebar on smaller screens, activated by a hamburger menu toggle. I need to ensure a consistent look and feel between devices. I\'m taking into account the desktop state as well, but with priority to the mobile behavior. I will look to requirement 6 and 7 to guide me!\n\n\n**Analyzing Layout Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m currently addressing fixed-width issues, specifically targeting the search bar\'s width and container padding. I\'m moving from hardcoded widths like `w-72` to flexible approaches using `flex-1` with `max-w` to allow the search bar to grow gracefully on larger screens without overflow. I\'m also adding a hamburger menu (`lg:hidden`) for the navigation drawer on mobile/tablet devices, as well as fixing unnecessary margins and fixed pixel widths on dashboard sections per requirements 1 and 2.\n\n\n**Optimizing Dashboard Layout**\n\nI\'m now revising the dashboard\'s responsive container. I\'ve pinpointed `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx` and am removing the `max-w-7xl` and `mx-auto` constraints, opting for `w-full min-w-0` with padding adjustments across screen sizes. The aim is to make the dashboard expand responsively to fill the viewport and accommodate variable screen sizes, ensuring the main content and dashboard consume available space.\n\n\n**Examining Security Page Layout**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx` component, specifically focusing on its responsiveness. I\'m prioritizing making this section full fluid width, using all the available viewport. I\'m analyzing the existing grid structure for the KPI cards and the middle section, paying close attention to column spans and applying `min-w-0` to the cards to prevent horizontal overflow. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s fully responsive to different screen sizes.\n\n\n**Adjusting Card Column Spans**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the layout of `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx`, specifically considering large screens. I\'ve noted the current card structure, with a left column housing two cards side-by-side and a right column stacking two cards vertically, creating a height discrepancy. I\'m exploring how to best adjust column spans and layouts to create a more balanced and responsive presentation, particularly on larger screens, guided by the requirements in section 8.\n\n\n**Structuring Dashboard Sections**\n\nI\'m now integrating the additional sections for Threat Types, Targeted Brands, and the AI Assistant into the dashboard. I\'m taking the user\'s suggested structure into account, and realizing I need to prioritize efficient use of available space across screen sizes. I\'m considering the current dashboard layout and ensuring all sections fit gracefully, particularly on the desktop, and considering the four cards in Section B.\n\n\n**Evaluating Column Spacing**\n\nI\'m now deep in adjusting the dashboard\'s layout, specifically considering the \"Live Investigation Activity\" and \"Geolocation\" sections. I\'m focusing on their height and how they\'ll fit alongside other sections on different screen sizes. Currently I\'m analyzing how these sections scale, especially if there\'s an additional section underneath \"Threat Overview\" and \"Email Volume Trend\". I\'m investigating how best to balance these sections in terms of column spacing and responsiveness, and especially on larger screens.\n\n\n**Refining Section Placement**\n\nI\'m now refining the placement of \"Live Investigation Activity\" and \"Geolocation\" sections, especially the structure under \"Threat Overview\" and \"Email Volume Trend.\" I noticed that the prior code\'s use of column spans and `space-y-6` left an empty vertical space. I\'m focusing on ensuring these sections are properly balanced and displayed.\n\n\n**Revising Case Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Recent Cases\" section and considering the suggested dashboard structure. The aim is to ensure it integrates seamlessly into the existing layout, focusing on the correct placement, and using the user\'s structure in section 7! I\'m resolving the empty space issue from the prior layouts with column spans, and adjusting the layout for wide screens.\n\n\n**Analyzing Section Placement**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the placement of the Geolocation section. I\'m focusing on the dashboard structure, weighing different options for integrating Geolocation while adhering to the layout constraints. I\'m carefully considering the existing structure and requirements to maximize viewport utilization and efficiency, and ensure all the other sections work well together.\n\n\n**Reorganizing Grid Structure**\n\nI\'m now revising the dashboard\'s middle grid layout, specifically for larger screens. I\'m experimenting with a 12-column grid structure, considering the placement of \"Threat Overview,\" \"Email Volume Trend,\" \"Live Investigation Activity,\" and \"Geolocation.\" I\'m evaluating different column spans to optimize their arrangement and make better use of available space.\n\n\n"
