  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Security Page Edits**\n\nI\'m currently working on a precise replacement for lines 221 to 682 of `SecurityOverviewPage.tsx`. The goal is to refine the middle section, encompassing the threat overview, email volume trends, live activity, and geolocation data. I\'m focusing on the exact edits needed for the code.\n\n\n**Restructuring UI Elements**\n\nI\'ve decided to restructure the section using a grid layout for better visual flow, focusing on a more modular card design. Specifically, I\'m adjusting the layout, switching from a split 8/4 column structure to a more flexible grid. I\'ve considered several factors to improve the user experience, focusing on a more cohesive presentation of threat overview, email volume, live activity, and geolocation data.\n\n\n**Implementing Threat Display Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the visual components for threat data, specifically the \"Threat Overview\" section. I\'m building out the time frame switcher (24h, 7d, 14d, 30d) using buttons that update the displayed threat period. I\'m also working on the bar graph elements, beginning with the \"Malicious\" threat type. I\'m considering the best UI elements for data presentation.\n\n\n**Designing Threat Percentage Bars**\n\nI\'m now implementing the threat percentage bars within the threat display. I\'ve focused on the \"malicious\", \"suspicious\", and \"benign\" threat types. Each bar includes a percentage value and a visual indicator representing the data. I\'m aiming for a clear and concise presentation.\n\n\n\n**Adding Inconclusive Threat Display**\n\nI\'ve just added the \"Inconclusive\" threat type to the percentage bar display. The code for it is complete, which mirrors the design for the \"Malicious\", \"Suspicious\", and \"Benign\" threats. I\'m focusing on ensuring it scales properly with varying percentages, using `Math.max` for a minimum width, and adding to the `activeThreats` data to use this display.\n\n\n**Adding Risk Posture Display**\n\nI\'ve just introduced the display for risk posture, including an icon, severity level, and a concise note about the current security standing. I\'ve focused on ensuring the visual elements integrate properly into the existing card design and will be dynamically updated. I\'ve also incorporated a dynamic email volume graph and a live investigation activity card within the same grid layout.\n\n\n**Integrating Live Investigation Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the live investigation activity component into the grid layout. I\'ve focused on displaying a dynamic timeline, including case ingestion data, using a concise format with timestamps and descriptions, making it easy to quickly check for updates and current events. I\'ve also incorporated a \"See all\" button for navigation.\n\n\n**Formatting Investigation Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on formatting the display for investigation events. I\'m aiming for a concise timeline format with timestamps, icons indicating threat level, and clear descriptions of events. I\'m paying close attention to the visual hierarchy, ensuring the data is easily scannable and readable, and implementing a small dot for visual cohesion.\n\n\n**Refining Activity Item Styles**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual style of individual activity items, focusing on concise time displays, threat indicators, and descriptive text. I\'m ensuring all data is easily scannable. I\'m also addressing the appearance of the threat-level indicators, ensuring they\'re clear.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Case Navigation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the navigation to the inbox from the \"Recent Cases\" section. I\'ve finished the component, and focused on making sure it will navigate to the inbox on click. I\'m also addressing the appearance of the threat level indicators.\n\n\n\n**Adding Table Display**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a table view for recent cases, featuring sortable columns for subject, sender, risk, status, and received time. The table includes visual indicators for risk level and the ability to view details. I\'m focusing on responsiveness.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Table Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding interactive elements to the table. Specifically, I\'m working on the row click functionality, making each row clickable to view case details. I\'ve also integrated hover states for visual feedback. I\'m focusing on user experience, and visual aesthetics.\n\n\n\n**Refining Table Interaction Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `handleCaseClick` functionality to open the case details when a row is clicked. I\'m ensuring it functions correctly for each row, and focusing on a seamless transition to the case view. I\'ve integrated this into the hover functionality for optimal UX.\n\n\n**Updating Table Column Styling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the table\'s column styles for enhanced readability. Specifically, I\'m adjusting the padding, font weights, and text colors to improve clarity and visual hierarchy, ensuring a streamlined and intuitive data presentation. I\'m also addressing the column widths to support the longest text while maintaining readability.\n\n\n**Enhancing Table Filtering**\n\nI\'m now integrating filtering capabilities into the recent cases table. I\'m focusing on allowing users to filter by various criteria such as risk level, status, and received time, enhancing data accessibility. I\'m exploring different filtering UI elements for the best user experience.\n\nI\'m adding options to filter by sender and subject to enable quick and easy searches, and implementing a robust filter, allowing a dynamic search for cases by subject, sender, risk, status, and receive time. I\'m aiming for an intuitive design. I\'ve completed the filters, and I\'m currently working on the backend, for data processing.\n\n\n**Implementing Table Interactions**\n\nI\'m now focused on enabling detailed case viewing when a row is clicked, specifically \'A2287\', in the recent case table. I\'m focusing on making a seamless transition to the case view, and testing for data consistency on interaction.\n\n\n**Finalizing Row Action Integration**\n\nCurrently, I\'m integrating the row action for case viewing; clicking \'A2287\' from the recent case table correctly redirects to the detailed case view. I\'ve confirmed all data is rendered as expected in the view.\n\n\n**Adding Geolocation Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating a geolocation display for malicious senders within the security overview. I\'m focusing on incorporating an interactive world map component, along with a time frame switcher. I\'ve designed the map with real geographic contours and attack hotspots. I\'m also adding in country statistics to view risk per country.\n\n\n**Integrating Country Risk Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating risk data per country, along with the map display. I\'m focusing on visually representing the risk associated with each country, based on threat data. The code integration is complete.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Styling**\n\nI\'m now refining the styling of the threat distribution display components. I\'m ensuring consistency in the visual presentation. I am also making sure that the data in the \"Malicious\", \"Suspicious\", and \"Others\" bars are rendered correctly, by reviewing the code above.\n\n\n\n"
