  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Investigation Layout**\n\nI\'ve been looking closely at the image of the investigation interface, specifically the top bar. The design\'s clear. It displays \"Investigation\" as the title, followed by a subtitle about deep analysis, clear evidence, and confident decisions. I also see a breadcrumb navigation showing the path back to the investigations list, and finally the case ID. Action buttons for re-investigation are also present.\n\n\n**Analyzing Theme Infrastructure**\n\nI\'ve been planning the implementation of dark and light modes for the app. The core focus is on establishing a robust theme infrastructure using Tailwind\'s `@custom-variant dark` for dark mode styling and CSS variables for smooth transitions. I will integrate a color-scheme variable and apply transition utilities to the body.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Switching**\n\nI\'ve added the `theme` property to the UI state and implemented logic to read user\'s theme preference from local storage or system settings, defaulting to light mode. I\'ve introduced `toggleTheme()` and `setTheme()` functions. Synchronization with the DOM\'s `dark` class is now in place and integrated on initial app load, with persistent storage. I\'m also planning the placement of the dark/light mode toggle in both the top bar, sidebar, and settings menu. I\'ll make sure to add tooltip labels and a keyboard shortcut.\n\n\n**Defining Color Specifications**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the color specifications for different components. I\'ve established light and dark mode styles for the app shell, top bar, sidebar, and cards across various views. I\'ve set the background, text, and input colors. I\'ve also detailed the colors for card backgrounds, borders, and inner dividers in both light and dark modes. I\'m focusing on consistency.\n\n\n**Detailing Visual Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing visual components across the dashboard and case pages, outlining color specifications for elements like metric cards, threat overviews, and the threat world map. For example, I\'ve outlined the color of the dark mode ocean, continents, and glowing dots on the map. I\'ve also specified colors for the recent cases table and threat types.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 726165971
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
