    thinking: "**Defining UI Theme**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating a `theme` property, either \"light\" or \"dark\", into the `UIState` object. I\'m now exploring how the application will detect the initial theme, considering environments where `window` isn\'t available. I\'m working through the logic for theme initialization now.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Persistence**\n\nI\'ve made progress on theme persistence. I\'m now leveraging `localStorage` to save the user\'s preferred theme, falling back to a dark theme default if none is stored, or if the environment does not support `localStorage`. I\'ve added a function `applyTheme` to update the DOM\'s class. I\'m also implementing functions to `setTheme` and `toggleTheme`, updating the UI store and the DOM.\n\n\n"
